findings.body:
The `From<tray_icon::MouseButtonState>` impl now maps `Up` to `MouseButtonState::Down` and `Down` to `MouseButtonState::Up`. This was not a clippy fix, and the base mapping was correct. Every tray click event sent to user code will report the opposite button state, which breaks any app that checks `button_state` to detect a press.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/tray/mod.rs" lines="31-38"}

Revert both arms to `Up => Up` and `Down => Down`. Consider adding a unit test that asserts the conversion, since nothing in this PR covers it.

The PR removes the `#[cfg(feature = "isolation")]` that sat on the `impl Default` block and leaves it on the `#[derive(Template)]` struct. The struct `PatternJavascript` is now compiled only when `isolation` is enabled. `manager/webview.rs` constructs `PatternJavascript` unconditionally at line 131 and imports it at line 25, so any build without the `isolation` feature will fail with an unresolved-name error.

::code{file="crates/tauri/src/pattern.rs" lines="76-81"}

::code{file="crates/tauri/src/manager/webview.rs" lines="128-133"}

The cfg was attached to the `impl Default` block in the base commit, and the struct was never gated. Remove the cfg from the struct and keep it only on `IsolationSide` and the `Default` derive, or follow the same gating pattern the call site uses.

The PR adds a new public constructor, `TrayIconEvent::new_click`, with a doc comment that says it is for testing. A clippy cleanup should not expand the public API of `tauri`, and once published this constructor becomes a semver commitment. It also hard-codes zeroed positions and sizes, which is probably not what a test that uses it would want.

::diff{file="crates/tauri/src/tray/mod.rs" lines="137-155"}

If the helper is needed by tests, make it `pub(crate)` and put it behind `#[cfg(test)]`, or move it into the test module. Otherwise drop it from this PR.
